es into a single exact binomial test (binomtest(15, 20, 0.5)), i.e., four repeated measurements per animal are treated as independent rows in a row-independent procedure — the issue is demonstrated in the selected report itself.\",\"The reported p = 0.0414 and its below-0.05 significance depend entirely on the inflated n = 20; the effective independent sample is 5 animals, so the report's conclusion of a demonstrated warm-arm preference is not supported by the workflow and data.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column salamander_id is consistent with data/input.csv: 20 rows cover five salamanders (SAL-01..SAL-05) with exactly four rows each, matching the data description; animals are the independent units in both the choice-count arm and the latency-averaging arm.","The report explicitly enters every scored release as an independent Bernoulli trial and pools all 20 releases into a single exact binomial test (binomtest(15, 20, 0.5)), i.e., four repeated measurements per animal are treated as independent rows in a row-independent procedure — the issue is demonstrated in the selected report itself.","The reported p = 0.0414 and its below-0.05 significance depend entirely on the inflated n = 20; the effective independent sample is 5 animals, so the report's conclusion of a demonstrated warm-arm preference is not supported by the workflow and data.","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":8403,"ttft_stream_ms":1741,"time_to_request_ms":15,"type":"result","duration_ms":20590,"uuid":"2a74a7cc-7786-4c93-b872-f2cb7b52031e"}
